# Files
# -----
*.bak
*.env
.env.*
!.env.*.sample
*.log
.hugo_build.lock
hugo_stats.json

# Personal, machine-specific Claude Code settings. The shared
# .claude/settings.json (if any) stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Directories
# -----------
node_modules/
public/
resources/
.netlify/
# Copied in at build time for non-production contexts only
# (bin/install-gate.mjs); production never has it.
netlify/edge-functions/

# Each agent's notes and files, and its local instructions (the
# bullpen: ~/Code/nff/docs/multi-agent-workflow.md). Never tracked.
.ignored/
CLAUDE.local.md

# Incident reports (docs/rollback.md). They name orders and customers
# and this repository is public, so they stay on disk. Only the README
# that says so is tracked.
incidents/*
!incidents/README.md

# Playwright's run output (npm run e2e).
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Vendored Hugo reference material. These are upstream snapshots, not
# our code — 169 MB that would sit in history forever. Re-clone them
# with the commands in docs/README.md. Ignoring them also protects them
# from `git clean -fd`, which skips ignored files.
docs/example-projects/
docs/hugo-docs-source/

# Written by the Netlify CLI when it serves functions locally.
deno.lock

# The originals James keeps beside the photos he exports for the site.
assets/images/*_original
